# Your own hosts for the remote-host guard (remoteHosts in .configs/vulcan.config.*).
# Copy this file to .agents/hooks/trusted-hosts.local - git ignores that file - and list your hosts there.
# That keeps host names out of the committed config.
#
# One host per line. A plain line is trusted for any command.
# A line that starts with "readonly:" allows only read-only commands (uptime, cat, kubectl get ...).
# A host is a name or a pattern with * (at least one letter or digit), or a $VARIABLE. Not a user, a path or a port.
#
# my-laptop.example
# readonly: db-replica.example
# readonly: *.prod.example
